"Denis" <denisdavidvalente@hotmail.com> wrote

> As a start, I would like to know:
> How damage is calculated. (is it just slashem, or does / did vanilla
> nethack have Showdamage?)

I don't know of any "showdamage" option in Nethack.

However, the Weapons spoiler explains damage fairly in detail, from your
own weapons:
http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/weap-341.html#calcdamage

I'm not sure how damage to you works, exactly.  I think it's essentially
the same as the above, only your armor class (if below 0) reduces damage
by d(AC).  So AC-20 reduces damage by d20, AC-60 reduces by d60, etc.
This makes very high negative AC quite useful, as most attacks do almost
no damage.

> How skill slots work, how many do you get, and what difference does it
> make to be skilled / expert etc.

The same weapons spoiler I linked above has a section on skill slots.

Essentially, they work based on how many times you've successfully hit
with a weapon or successfully cast a spell.  After 20 hits / casts you can
go to basic, 80 lets you get to skilled, etc.

You get as many skill slots as you have experience levels (and your XL is
capped at 30.)

> What different effects does each and every spell have with the various
> skill levels.

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/spl2-341.html explains these in
detail.

It would be nice to put together some of these answers in more specific
FAQs or spoilers -- in particular, an AC FAQ would be nice.  But hopefully
I've given you at least a couple useful answers.

Try http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/spoilerlist.html for a very
extensive spoiler list ;)  If it's not there, it's probably nowhere.



